--- D5 universality of A (must be window-length independent) ---
  A(L=50)/A(L=25) = 0.19  (ln ratio -1.69 +- 1.34, z = -1.3)
  [PASS] D5 universality of A: ln[A(L=50)/A(L=25)] = -1.69 +- 1.34 (|z| = 1.3 < 2) -> L-dependence NOT refuted, but per-leg SE of ln A ~ 0.6 means A is only determined to ~e^0.6: LOW POWER -- universality is unconstrained, not established

--- 2b Milgrom check: nu = sqrt(1 + 1/y), y = rho_bar/A ---
  A fixed = 3.764e-02; y = rho_bar/A in [12, 20] (huge -> nu_model-1 = 1/2y in [2.45e-02, 4.10e-02])
  chi2 = 68.7 on df = 28 -> chi2/df = 2.45, p = 2.86e-05
  (sigma_nu uses the bare GUE asymptotic number-variance ln(L rho)/pi^2; the
   standard form adds ln(2pi)+const terms (~1.7x at these L rho), which would
   bring chi2/df toward ~1 -- i.e. the deviations are ordinary GUE noise,
   not a RAR signal, under either reading)
  signal/noise = median|nu_model-1| / median sigma_nu = 8.66e-01
  [FAIL] D7 informativeness gate: S = 8.66e-01 <= 1 -> UNINFORMATIVE: the Milgrom form is indistinguishable from nu = 1 at these y (chi2/df ~ 1 would then be the NULL, not a RAR validation)

--- diagnostic (not gated): the S-shift delta_n = gamma_n - N^-1(n) ---
  rms(delta_n * rho) = 0.5008 (S-fluctuation amplitude scale; GUE expectation ~ (1/pi) sqrt(ln n) scale ~ 0.1-0.3)

